A||||3||Motorhead||'88 Dash in an '84||||1||
Z||000000||Motorhead||05-16-2000||06:00 PM||||<BR>Are these interchangeable?  This '84 I just bought seems to be in a world of its own.||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||05-16-2000||10:13 PM||||All Fiero dashes are identical, so you can put an '88 dash into an '84, if you so desire.<P>The only differences are the color schemes.  Some are 2 tone some are solid and if it's tan, then there were different shades ('84-'85, '86-'87 & '88), plus some were 2-tone and some were solid!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Motorhead||05-17-2000||02:12 AM||||I thought so. Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||05-17-2000||09:35 AM||||All fiero body and interior items interchange thru all years.<P>I just did this job as part of installing the wiring for the power mirrors.<P>I replaced a solid dark grey dash with 2 tone one. (dark with light dyed front) It needs a little work but at least it's not broke.<P>Plan on a couple hours at least.<P>The frame for the console doesn't have to be removed, but you have to watch out for 2 small tabs that align the top ot the plastic radio & a/c frame to the air duct opening in the dash. You do have to remove the metal frame that ties the dash to the console.<P>make sure all the dash pod wiring is in the clear before installing any screws in the new dash.||||reg||1
